{"assets":["/statement-assets/95f9ded7e1ae98bdc4e5fa7c2bedf27c3580a99b48b69d64921b70f5cede7ca6.png","/statement-assets/231fe5a4750322cf7718f0603bd03de39b41701d810de5a0463604a0ab1d20d0.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1552","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Colors and Intervals"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The numbers $$$1, \\, 2, \\, \\dots, \\, n \\cdot k$$$ are colored with $$$n$$$ colors. These colors are indexed by $$$1, \\, 2, \\, \\dots, \\, n$$$. For each $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$, there are exactly $$$k$$$ numbers colored with color $$$i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$[a, \\, b]$$$ denote the interval of integers between $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ inclusive, that is, the set $$$\\{a, \\, a + 1, \\, \\dots, \\, b\\}$$$. You must choose $$$n$$$ intervals $$$[a_1, \\, b_1], \\, [a_2, \\, b_2], \\, \\dots, [a_n, \\, b_n]$$$ such that: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" for each $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$, it holds $$$1 \\le a_i \\lt b_i \\le n \\cdot k$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" for each $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$, the numbers $$$a_i$$$ and $$$b_i$$$ are colored with color $$$i$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" each number $$$1 \\le x \\le n \\cdot k$$$ belongs to at most $$$\\left\\lceil \\frac{n}{k - 1} \\right\\rceil$$$ intervals. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One can show that such a family of intervals always exists under the given constraints."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 100$$$, $$$2 \\le k \\le 100$$$) — the number of colors and the number of occurrences of each color."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n \\cdot k$$$ integers $$$c_1, \\, c_2, \\, \\dots, \\, c_{nk}$$$ ($$$1 \\le c_j \\le n$$$), where $$$c_j$$$ is the color of number $$$j$$$. It is guaranteed that, for each $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$, it holds $$$c_j = i$$$ for exactly $$$k$$$ distinct indices $$$j$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output $$$n$$$ lines. The $$$i$$$-th line should contain the two integers $$$a_i$$$ and $$$b_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple valid choices of the intervals, output any."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 3\n2 4 3 1 1 4 2 3 2 1 3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 5\n1 7\n8 11\n6 12"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"chi